# Independently authored PG maint/session/ownership
# DDL sentinel slice for the GPL MTR-format runner.
# NOT copied or adapted from MySQL's mysql-test/.
#
# Existing coverage (do NOT duplicate):
#   - CHECKPOINT, DISCARD (ALL/TEMP/TEMPORARY/PLANS/
#     SEQUENCES), REASSIGN OWNED, DROP OWNED, SECURITY
#     LABEL, ALTER DATABASE, ALTER OPERATOR: ZERO prior
#     coverage. Wide-grep for each keyword returns no
#     hits.
#
# Pre-existing rejection shape patterns:
#   - Shape (d) — "Expected: an SQL statement, found:
#     <KW>" at column 1 (PR #371 et al.).
#   - Shape (c) — "unsupported statement: sqlparser::
#     ast::Statement" (PR #371 mysql_maintenance_cmds_
#     sentinel:79-83).
#   - "DROP restricted-list" — "Expected: CONNECTOR,
#     DATABASE, ... after DROP, found: <KW>" (PR #391/
#     #395 + temp_table_basic_extra:91).
#   - "CREATE/ALTER OPERATOR partial-grammar" — "Expected:
#     (, found: =" (PR #390 Shape C with CREATE OPERATOR
#     at col 19; this slice extends to ALTER OPERATOR
#     at col 18).
#
# This slice pins:
#
#   Shape (d) — CHECKPOINT / REASSIGN OWNED / SECURITY
#   LABEL (3 keywords at col 1):
#     - sqlparser doesn't recognize these as statement-
#       level keywords. Adds 3 new keywords to the
#       shape (d) bucket alongside HANDLER/SHUTDOWN/
#       IMPORT/MOVE/CLUSTER.
#
#   Shape (c) — DISCARD ALL/TEMP/TEMPORARY/PLANS/
#   SEQUENCES (5 forms):
#     - sqlparser parses DISCARD into AST, zeta
#       dispatcher has no arm, falls through to
#       convert.rs:432 catch-all with internal type
#       name leak.
#
#   "DROP restricted-list" — DROP OWNED BY (2 forms):
#     - "Expected: ... after DROP, found: OWNED" at
#       column 6. Same fingerprint as PR #395 (with
#       TEXT keyword). New OWNED keyword.
#
#   Shape C — ALTER OPERATOR partial-grammar (1 form):
#     - "Expected: (, found: =" at column 18. sqlparser
#       has an ALTER OPERATOR keyword arm (gets past
#       `ALTER OPERATOR ===`), but doesn't parse the
#       definition body. Same Shape C fingerprint as PR
#       #390 CREATE OPERATOR (col 19); new keyword
#       (ALTER instead of CREATE) at col 18.
#
#   DOCUMENTED INTENTIONAL COMPAT NO-OP — ALTER DATABASE:
#     - All three ALTER DATABASE forms (OWNER TO,
#       RENAME TO, SET) silently succeed with NO ERROR.
#     - This is NOT a BUG — it is a documented
#       intentional compat shim. Source witnesses:
#         - zeta-parser/src/lib.rs:155 — comment
#           "Handle ALTER DATABASE (accepted as no-op
#           for compatibility)"
#         - zeta-parser/src/ast.rs:272 — doc-comment
#           "ALTER DATABASE ... (accepted as no-op
#           for compatibility)"
#         - zeta-server/src/lib.rs:15199-15202 —
#           handler with "No-op for compatibility."
#         - zeta-server/tests/multi_database.rs:185
#           — `test_alter_database_noop` explicitly
#           tests it succeeds without error
#     - Pinned here so the compat behavior is visible
#       on the MySQL wire as well. Applies symmetric
#       reading of the wire-divergence memory: just as
#       no-error doesn't prove SUPPORT, silent-no-op
#       doesn't prove BUG — must check engine source
#       first. Same NoOp category as Statement::Copy
#       and AlterIndex at convert.rs:425-427.
#
# Big-picture finding:
#
#   The PG maint/session/ownership surface has FOUR
#   distinct rejection routes (shape (d), shape (c),
#   DROP restricted-list, Shape C partial-grammar) +
#   ONE documented intentional compat no-op (ALTER
#   DATABASE). All four shape mechanisms are pre-
#   existing; novelty is per-keyword surface plus the
#   ALTER DATABASE no-op pin.
#
#   Apps porting PG operational/maintenance scripts:
#     - CHECKPOINT, DISCARD ALL/etc, REASSIGN OWNED,
#       SECURITY LABEL, DROP OWNED, ALTER OPERATOR
#       all fail at parse — drop from scripts.
#     - ALTER DATABASE returns success without doing
#       anything (documented intentional behavior).
#       Apps relying on ALTER DATABASE for actual
#       database-state mutation should rebuild the DB
#       and use GRANT for ownership instead — but they
#       can expect no error from the migration script.
#
# Adaptation notes:
#   # zeta-adapt: KNOWN GAP — CHECKPOINT, REASSIGN
#     OWNED, SECURITY LABEL all error 1064 at shape (d).
#   # zeta-adapt: KNOWN GAP — DISCARD (ALL/TEMP/TEMPORARY/
#     PLANS/SEQUENCES) all error 1064 at shape (c).
#   # zeta-adapt: KNOWN GAP — DROP OWNED BY errors 1064
#     at DROP restricted-list ("found: OWNED").
#   # zeta-adapt: KNOWN GAP — ALTER OPERATOR partial-
#     grammar (parallel to CREATE OPERATOR Shape C from
#     PR #390).
#   # zeta-adapt: INTENTIONAL COMPAT NO-OP — ALTER
#     DATABASE silently succeeds without effect
#     (zeta-server/src/lib.rs:15199 — "No-op for
#     compatibility"). Database-management migrations
#     can expect no error but no mutation either.

--echo === Shape (d) — CHECKPOINT / REASSIGN OWNED / SECURITY LABEL → "found: <KW>" at col 1 ===

--error 1064
CHECKPOINT;
--error 1064
REASSIGN OWNED BY alice TO bob;
--error 1064
SECURITY LABEL ON TABLE t IS 'classified';
--error 1064
SECURITY LABEL FOR provider ON TABLE t IS 'classified';

--echo === Shape (c) — DISCARD ALL/TEMP/TEMPORARY/PLANS/SEQUENCES (catch-all internal-type leak) ===

--error 1064
DISCARD ALL;
--error 1064
DISCARD TEMP;
--error 1064
DISCARD TEMPORARY;
--error 1064
DISCARD PLANS;
--error 1064
DISCARD SEQUENCES;

--echo === DROP restricted-list — DROP OWNED BY (2 forms) → "found: OWNED" at col 6 ===

--error 1064
DROP OWNED BY alice;
--error 1064
DROP OWNED BY alice CASCADE;

--echo === Shape C — ALTER OPERATOR partial-grammar → "Expected: (, found: =" at col 18 ===

# sqlparser has an ALTER OPERATOR arm — parses past
# `ALTER OPERATOR ===` then fails at the definition
# body. Parallel to CREATE OPERATOR Shape C from PR
# #390 (which fires at col 19 for `CREATE OPERATOR`).
--error 1064
ALTER OPERATOR === (INT, INT) OWNER TO bob;

--echo === INTENTIONAL COMPAT NO-OP — ALTER DATABASE silently succeeds (documented in zeta source) ===

# DOCUMENTED INTENTIONAL — not a bug. zeta source:
#   - zeta-parser/src/lib.rs:155 (comment)
#   - zeta-parser/src/ast.rs:272 (doc-comment)
#   - zeta-server/src/lib.rs:15199-15202 (handler:
#     "No-op for compatibility.")
#   - zeta-server/tests/multi_database.rs:185
#     (`test_alter_database_noop` asserts success)
# All three forms succeed without error or mutation:
ALTER DATABASE myapp OWNER TO bob;
ALTER DATABASE myapp RENAME TO renamed_target;
ALTER DATABASE myapp SET search_path = public;
